# Accounts and sync. Both of these ship inside the bundle and are meant to:
# the URL names the project, and the publishable key names the project rather
# than the person. Row-level security is what protects the data — see
# supabase/README.md. Never put a secret key (sb_secret_… or service_role) in a
# VITE_ variable; it bypasses RLS and would reach every visitor.
# Leave both unset and the app works exactly as it does now, storing locally.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
